# Rule 6 of the product direction (issue #3; QUESTIONS Q17), on a Mac as it comes (rule 1): drags must never block input.
# Story: the same as in rule-6-drags-never-hold-the-mouse.sim, with macOS's own tiling on. The left, right and top edges of the screen are
# macOS's then (Q23), so the windows are dragged to what stays Arbor's: the bottom edge and the edges of docked windows.
# However a drag ends, whoever takes the window, nothing of Arbor's is left on the screen that could take the next click.
quiet
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
# The keys work at every setting.
dock 101 left
expect docked 101
# The bottom edge is Arbor's.
drag 102 1000 897
expect docked 102
expect preview none
# Let go at once, before any target has woken up.
drag 103 300 850 quick
expect preview none
# With ⌘ nothing docks and nothing is offered.
drag 103 1000 897 cmd
expect floating 103
expect preview none
# It lies at the bottom edge now. Taken hold of there and only nudged, it has not been carried to that edge: nothing is offered.
pick-up 103 1010 897
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 103
drag 103 1100 200
expect floating 103
# Out of a slot and back onto the Desktop.
drag 102 1000 300
expect floating 102
expect preview none
# Dropped on another window's edge.
drag 102 300 850
expect docked 102
expect preview none
# The control: while a window is held over a target of Arbor's there is a preview to lose.
pick-up 103 1000 897
expect preview showing
let-go
expect docked 103
expect preview none
# Along macOS's edges there is none to lose, on the way there or at the last point, and none afterwards.
float 103
pick-up 103 1435 400
expect preview none
let-go
expect floating 103
expect preview none
pick-up 103 1439 400
expect preview none
let-go
wait 1
expect floating 103
expect preview none
pick-up 103 700 0
expect preview none
let-go
wait 1
expect floating 103
expect preview none
# Arbor is paused with a window in the hand, over a target of its own.
pick-up 103 1000 897
expect preview showing
pause
expect preview none
let-go
resume
expect preview none
